  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on comparing the minimum probabilities of the lotteries and prefers the one with the lower minimum probability (i.e., Lottery B with 20% vs. Lottery A with 100%). However, the individual’s reasoning emphasizes avoiding risk and valuing certainty, which is conceptually opposite to favoring a lottery because it has a lower minimum probability (which in this case means a non-zero chance of getting nothing). The individual considered the 20% chance of nothing as a negative aspect, whereas the decision reason would see that same 20% as a feature that makes Lottery B preferable due to its lower minimum probability. Thus, the information considered by the individual (certainty, risk aversion) does not align with the information emphasized by the decision reason (minimum probability values). Moreover, the individual’s justification is based on security and aversion to zero outcomes, which contradicts the logic of the decision reason. Therefore, it is certain that the individual did not use this decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
